1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,500
The plant and twin intentionally differ.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,538
The plant is a two-RC model.

3
00:00:04,538 --> 00:00:12,038
Its resistance follows an Arrhenius temperature law, and it has two thermal nodes, core and surface, plus aging drift.

4
00:00:12,038 --> 00:00:15,631
The twin is a one-RC model with a single thermal node.

5
00:00:15,631 --> 00:00:22,597
Its voltage is OCV of state of charge, minus current times R zero, minus the RC polarization.

6
00:00:22,597 --> 00:00:28,555
State of charge integrates current; the thermal node balances Joule heating against convection.

7
00:00:28,555 --> 00:00:31,553
The twin does not trust the initial state of charge.

8
00:00:31,553 --> 00:00:35,157
It starts at sixty percent while the plant starts at ninety-five.

9
00:00:35,157 --> 00:00:40,703
An extended Kalman filter estimates SoC, RC voltage, and surface temperature.

10
00:00:40,703 --> 00:00:48,871
A recursive least-squares tracker updates resistance, and a short-window regression separates a resistance change from a voltage-sensor offset.

11
00:00:48,871 --> 00:00:53,264
State of health is nominal resistance divided by estimated resistance.

12
00:00:53,264 --> 00:01:01,007
Offline, parameters are identified from HPPC data using least squares on measured voltage, current, and temperature only.

13
00:01:01,007 --> 00:01:04,065
The fit is eight point eight millivolts RMS.

